{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790544677,"nonce":"YWeiyuue9XKJ7TrC7nEt6k/HCfU=","title":"wasm: a compiled Wren→Haxe call should be a direct call","message":"A Wren→Haxe call in a wasm program costs about 280 ns (static), where a compiled Wren→Wren static costs 7 ns. Decompiled (wasm-tools print) from the interop fixtures' program, one `Bench.add(s)` in Tally.haxeStatic's loop is:\n\n1. The call site calls `wren_call_1` (WrenLift's runtime dispatch, about 2700 lines of wasm: callsite inline caches, env-flag OnceLocks, dispatch_call_rooted, a call_indirect to the member's entry, fiber actions), not the member. A compiled Wren static gets a direct call; a foreign member does not, though its symbol is known when the module compiles.\n2. `wlift_foreign_0_0_24__entry(args, argc)` loads the arguments back from a memory array and calls the export.\n3. Ash's export `caribou_4haxe_5Bench_5Bench_t3add_1`: hlp_setup_trap_jit, __wasm_setjmp inside a try_table (LLVM's wasm SjLj), hlp_remove_trap_jit, on every call; and the fiber transform's unwind/rewind instrumentation around all of it, since the trap calls put the thunk in the suspend set.\n4. Its body: `add` itself inlined to one f64.add, but out-of-line calls to caribou_wren_to_float and caribou_wren_from_float (five to ten instructions each, in caribou's runtime object, so nothing inlines them across objects) and an hlp_shadow_push / hlp_shadow_pop pair around a frame that holds no references.\n\nWhat it should be: the loop calls the export directly, and the export is the NaN-box conversion, the add, and the conversion back, with a throw costing only when it happens.\n\nOwners: 1–2 WrenLift (a call on a class bound to a foreign module's class calls the member's symbol directly, as a compiled static is called); 3 Ash (trap as wasm try/catch, b710dcc99a08194a8b73354fc34e794eeab1cbbefc397fff79b7997e084aed58; the thunk then leaves the suspend set); 4 Ash's shadow frame for a body with no references, and the casts, which Ash can inline only if it has them.","files":null}]}